From: oneplus-nord2t-karen contributors <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 03:31:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sched_assist: use an explicit void prototype

Clang treats old-style empty parameter lists as errors in this kernel's
warning-as-error build. This function takes no arguments; express that
directly without changing its behavior.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
---
 vendor/oplus/kernel/oplus_performance/sched_assist/sched_assist_common.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/vendor/oplus/kernel/oplus_performance/sched_assist/sched_assist_common.h b/vendor/oplus/kernel/oplus_performance/sched_assist/sched_assist_common.h
index ce20f90..0ac3bc4 100644
--- a/vendor/oplus/kernel/oplus_performance/sched_assist/sched_assist_common.h
+++ b/vendor/oplus/kernel/oplus_performance/sched_assist/sched_assist_common.h
@@ -322 +322 @@
-static inline bool is_sched_assist_scene() {
+static inline bool is_sched_assist_scene(void) {
